{"id": "EUVD-2026-101133", "enisaUuid": "ab667d01-bd8f-3467-90dd-128a4bf86a54", "description": "vgmstream through r2117 contains a stack out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the G.722.1/Siren14 decoder in g7221_lib.c, whose bit reader refills without checking the data_u32 array end. Attackers can supply crafted .s14 or .sss files that drive decode_vector_quantized_mlt_indices() past the stack buffer during format detection, crashing the application.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T15:01:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:16:17", "baseScore": 4.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/vgmstream-g7221-bitreader-oob-read", "https://github.com/vgmstream/vgmstream/blob/71e2361042531fe767fb98300cf8c1ee95e539a0/src/coding/libs/g7221_lib.c#L838", "https://github.com/vgmstream/vgmstream", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vgmstream-through-r2117-stack-out-of-bounds-read-via-g-722.1-siren14-decoder"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110660", "GHSA-gvx8-xp47-575f"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "dc37b891-b901-32e8-aea7-79c17d3a96f8", "product": {"name": "vgmstream", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u2264r2117"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "881ce4fc-60d4-3f12-9138-a44ab4f59239", "vendor": {"name": "vgmstream"}}], "isExploited": false}